            "current": "Read both complete DE/EN cases. ASS has free acid and ester, ibuprofen acid, paracetamol phenol and amide.600/360/500g and1.2/1.8/1.0 tablets per person are correct. Case2 gives X1.5, Y2.0 tablets/person/30days and150g each X ingredient,320g ibuprofen. Historical RKI measurements remain distinct from fabricated sales, OTC-only scope and current prevalence.2.2 percentage points/22% relative change is correct. IQWiG supports the bounded application distinctions; molecular structure alone does not establish clinical interchangeability. Current independently inspected native page, source/prerequisite context and materials support this unchanged complete profile. Frozen first judgment: curricula/DE/Gymnasium/quality/goal-evidence/2026-10-16/chemie-native9-current437-fresh-independent-a-20261016-v1/FIRST.independent-current-nine-science-and-separate699.frozen.json sha256:dbdbefe4b37fa1dc2d314b647d1a275d81715783a9c2b6c76ef17ce846d97d4a"
